BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d4d2dcc5ee35d4e8fa6775ad6ff9b15cbe88b910@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261031T193113Z
DTSTART:20261115T180000Z
DTEND:20261115T200000Z
SUMMARY:Behind the Screen: La Bola Negra
LOCATION:West Newton Cinema\, 1296 Washington St\, Newton\, MA 02465
DESCRIPTION:LA BOLA NEGRA\, the bold new film from Spanish writer-directors
  Javier Calvo and Javier Ambrossi\, won the Best Director award at Cannes 
 and the People's Choice award at the Toronto International Film Festival. 
 Inspired by the surviving pages of an unfinished play by Federico García 
 Lorca and by Alberto Conejero's award-winning play La piedra oscura\, the 
 film tells the interconnected stories of three gay men in Spain in 1932\, 
 1937\, and 2017. Moving from the years before the Spanish Civil War\, thro
 ugh the war itself\, to the present day\, LA BOLA NEGRA is a sweeping\, pa
 ssionate triptych about desire\, repression\, historical memory\, and what
  one generation carries forward to the next.\nhttps://www.westnewtoncinema
 .com/movie/behind-the-screen-la-bola-negra\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://p
 ushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.westnewtoncinema.com/movie/behind-the-screen-la-bola-negra
END:VEVENT
