BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:61c34e6611a6270b676ffc252882788b8dcb5473@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261031T193113Z
DTSTART:20261119T233000Z
DTEND:20261120T013000Z
SUMMARY:Behind the Screen: Once Upon a Time in Harlem
LOCATION:West Newton Cinema\, 1296 Washington St\, Newton\, MA 02465
DESCRIPTION:ONCE UPON A TIME IN HARLEM captures an extraordinary evening in
  1972\, when pioneering documentarian William Greaves gathered surviving l
 uminaries of the Harlem Renaissance at Duke Ellington's Harlem townhouse. 
 Over four hours\, artists\, writers\, and intellectuals\, many of whom had
  not seen one another in fifty years\, reminisced\, argued\, laughed\, and
  debated their place in a rapidly changing cultural landscape. Greaves con
 sidered it the most important event he ever filmed. Decades later\, his so
 n David Greaves\, one of the original camera operators\, restored the 16mm
  footage and completed the film\, creating both a vivid time capsule and a
  searching inquiry into one of the most creative periods in American histo
 ry.\nhttps://www.westnewtoncinema.com/movie/behind-the-screen-once-upon-a-
 time-in-harlem\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.westnewtoncinema.com/movie/behind-the-screen-once-upon-a-ti
 me-in-harlem
END:VEVENT
